{"school":{"dbn":"20K939","name":"Sunset School of Cultural Learning","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"20","district_label":"District 20","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EC|EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"K-5","status":"open","enrollment":269,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"270 59 Street, Brooklyn, NY 11220","phone":"347-464-5131","website":"WWW.PS939.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/66885","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"PS 939 provides a rigorous, well-rounded educational program that fosters the development of literate, creative and culturally aware learners.  The school community creates an environment that promotes excellence in academic achievement, in which students strive to meet or exceed the Next Generation Learning Standards.  This is evident in the fact that 98% of our families responded favorably to inclusive leadership with teachers, parents, community leaders and students.  97% of our families responded favorably to strong family-community ties. and 98% of families responded favorably to trusting the principal and teachers.  \nIt is the goal of P.S. 939 to encourage a love of learning through innovative and challenging programs.  The school's reading curriculum is HMH Into Reading, EnVisions Math, Amplify, Passports and Civics for All. \nP.S. 939 has fostered partnerships with Marquis Studios and LOTUS to enrich the educational experiences for our students.  P.S. 939 also partnered with Grandma's Love which backpacks of food for families in need, also stocking our food pantry for the families of our school that are in need.  Our school also has a state-of-the-art dental clinic for our students and a robust after-school program to meet the needs of our families.\n This school has ASD Nest: Open to students currently enrolled in the ASD (Autism Spectrum Disorder) Nest program. If you are applying to ASD programs for the first time, please visit www.schools.nyc.gov/specializedprogram